{"type":"finding","id":"f-iter005-001","severity":"P1","label":"Forced interruption can strand a partial apply behind a lock that blocks the documented rollback. release-update.cjs creates .skilled/release/.apply.lock with exclusive creation and records its pid/start time (1775-1794); target writes are one at a time after rollback.json is saved (1889-1902), and ordinary lock cleanup is in finally (1903-1905). Inference: SIGKILL or forced termination bypasses that cleanup. The apply workflow refuses any pre-existing lock and says not to remove it (doctor-update-apply.yaml:98, 129-131), while rollback itself must acquire the same lock (release-update.cjs:2035-2059). An interruption can therefore leave a partial checkout with no documented way to reach rollback; terminal state logging is also bypassed (doctor-update-apply.yaml:191-195). Add verified stale-owner recovery that preserves the rollback path, plus interruption recovery coverage.","iteration":5,"sources":[".skilled/commands/doctor/scripts/release-update.cjs",".skilled/commands/doctor/assets/doctor-update-apply.yaml"]}
{"type":"finding","id":"f-iter005-002","severity":"P2","label":"The documented deployment models leave copied .skilled trees without a clear acquisition or sync route. PUBLIC-RELEASE.md says consumers use an .opencode symlink and that the old sync step is eliminated (3, 21-28, 74-76); .skilled/bin/README.md describes git-sync.sh as CI/live-branch publication (27), and .skilled/scripts/README.md lists install-git-hooks.sh for Git-hook installation (16, 22-28). Yet /doctor:update explicitly covers first use after copying or installing .skilled and explains only base recording (update.md:68; doctor-update-presentation.txt:82-88). Clarify whether copied trees are supported and where an operator gets and applies the next release.","iteration":5,"sources":["PUBLIC-RELEASE.md",".skilled/bin/README.md",".skilled/scripts/README.md",".skilled/commands/doctor/update.md",".skilled/commands/doctor/assets/doctor-update-presentation.txt"]}
{"type":"finding","id":"f-iter005-003","severity":"P2","label":"The release-note index points operators at a stale latest/upcoming version: it says current top-level entries end at v4.0.0.2 and calls .2 upcoming (.skilled/changelog/skilled/README.md:22-25), while the v4.0.0.3 release entry exists (.skilled/changelog/skilled/v4.0.0.3.md:2, 12). Refresh the index so installed-release identification and release-note lookup are unambiguous.","iteration":5,"sources":[".skilled/changelog/skilled/README.md",".skilled/changelog/skilled/v4.0.0.3.md"]}
